{"name":"Manila","hex":"#e7c9a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Manila","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The capital city of the Philippines; the regional capital of Metro Manila, in the island of Luzon.","Metro Manila, the National Capital Region (NCR)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Venerupis philippinarum; a Pacific clam.","Alternative form of manila (“kind of cheroot”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Manila"}],"entries":[{"title":"Manila","blocks":[{"text":"Manila, officially the City of Manila, is the capital and second-most populous city of the Philippines after Quezon City. According to the 2024 census, it has a population of 1,902,590 people. Located on the eastern shore of Manila Bay on the island of Luzon, it is classified as a highly urbanized city. With 44,935 inhabitants per square kilometer (116,380/sq mi), Manila is one of the world's most densely populated cities proper."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Cityscape_of_Manila%2C_2025_%2801%29.jpg/330px-Cityscape_of_Manila%2C_2025_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manila","wikidata":"Q1461"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Rizal_Monument.jpg/500px-Rizal_Monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Rizal_Monument.jpg/1280px-Rizal_Monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Rizal_Monument.jpg/500px-Rizal_Monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARizal_Monument.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Gate_of_Fort_Santiago_-_38923-Manila_%28352012